# Classic recursive SI workflow

Same review model as fortress-ai (see sibling `fortress-ai/.cursor/rules/recursive-si-workflow.mdc`).

## Classic pipeline

- **Scan**: `utils/integrity_diagnostics.py` (drift rollback, evolution staleness, cron heartbeats, fortress-ai sibling findings)
- **Queue**: `utils/si_recommendation_queue.py` → `data/si_recommendation_queue.json`
- **Evolve**: `agents/recursive_evolution.py` phase-1 runs scan + queue on each cycle (17:10 ET cron)

## Agent review

1. Read `data/si_recommendation_summary.json` and fortress-ai sibling summary when present
2. Triage `pending_agent_review` — recommend to user; wait for go-ahead before code changes
3. Policy auto-recovery: `maybe_clear_forced_rollback_on_recovery()` runs at end of evolve when metrics allow

## When fixing classic Fortress

- Extend `utils/integrity_diagnostics.py` with a new `code` and recommendation text
- Wire auto-action in evolve or policy guardrails where safe
- Run `./scripts/e2e_before_deploy.sh` before commit
